## Where submit_slurm's reused ssh/scp connections keep their control socket
## for a submission's staging calls (the mkdir and the scp -- not sbatch
## itself; see class/remote_exec.php's CONTROL_DIR comment for why sbatch is
## never multiplexed). Same per-account subdirectory reasoning as the
## breaker directory above. dbutils#45 step 5 provisions this directory
## 3770 us3:<web group> (the sticky bit so an account's own subdirectory,
## once created, cannot be renamed or removed by the other account). Set to
## '' to turn multiplexing off outright and have every call connect plainly,
## same as when the directory cannot be created or fails its checks.
##
## Only characters an absolute Unix path actually needs are accepted:
## letters, digits, '.', '_', '-' and '/'. Anything else (including a
## trailing newline) is refused the same as an unset directory, rather than
## being passed through to ssh's -o ControlPath, which splits on whitespace
## and '=', expands '%' sequences, and (OpenSSH 8.7+, EL9) rejects a "'".

